<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  XenotypeCut_NonSW_SpawnSets.xml - NONSW_XENOTYPES_SCOPE_1. Owner, question card 2026-10-09:
  cut all the remaining non-Star-Wars xenotypes, same rule as the twelve
  (XenotypeCut_SpawnSets.xml); repoint raider xenotype sets.

  The 31 the load-13+ def dump holds beyond our own, the twelve and Baseliner: Alpha Genes 15,
  Phytokin 3, det.* 6, Beliar, Highborn, Orc Clan, VRE Archon, VRE Fungoid, Titan, BigSmall's
  Frost Jotun in Blue. Each is removed from every xenotypeSet (FactionDef and PawnKindDef,
  abstract parents included); the unassigned chance falls to Baseliner, exactly as for the
  twelve. Factions whose whole set was a cut xenotype (KAR_OrcClan, VRE_Archons,
  AG_XenohumanPirates, AG_OutlanderCivilUnion, DV_OutlanderRoughBuzzer, DV_PirateKeshig) are
  already zeroed out of world creation by FactionSlate/OnlyOurFactions.xml, and none of them
  is on the canonical save's world.

  The def cut itself is Cherry Picker's (typed keys in
  infrastructure/state/cherrypicker/CherryPicker.SHIP.xml), EXCEPT the five whose names are
  compiled into their own mod's assembly (VRE_Archon, VRE_Fungoid, VRE_Gauranlenkin,
  VRE_Animakin, VRE_Poluxkin): those defs stay, unreachable (this file plus their companion
  genes cut), until their mods are retired.

  XenotypeChance loads by NODE NAME, and a Remove that matches nothing logs red, so each
  Remove sits inside a Conditional on the same xpath.
  Guarded by src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/selftest_xenotype_cut_nonsw.py.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/*/xenotypeSet/xenotypeChances/BX_Beliar</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>Defs/*/xenotypeSet/xenotypeChances/BX_Beliar</xpath>
